title: Orchestration + task-system self-audit → v7 "close the loop" thesis
summary: Two back-to-back 5-lens team audits (task system, then the orchestration engine itself) proved with file:line evidence that Paradigm "records that it was asked to do the right thing but does not verify it did." The findings from both slices converged on one keystone — a persisted, claimant-owned task DAG — and reframed v7 from "build a PM tool" to "close the orchestration/learning loop so the framework's own checks actually prove true."
