learnings:
  - 'Classifier (orchestration.ts:2341-2374) is a substring keyword ladder with a ''bugfix poison-pill'': any task containing fix/error/broken/fails is vetoed from ''analysis'' and routed to bugfix→[security,builder]. Reproduced live: this analysis session was misclassified as bugfix.'
  - The team's richest agents (North/product, Loid/forge, Scout/researcher, Helix/dx) are NOT in the paradigm_agent_prompt routable enum (orchestration.ts:843) — auto-orchestration structurally cannot assemble its best team.
  - 'The learning loop is open at two joints in BOTH execution worlds (MCP persona-adoption vs CLI real-spawn): task_done feeds nothing, and debrief→postflight is advisory prose not a wired call. Postflight runs 2>/dev/null & and processes zero entries without manual nomination engagement — broken state is byte-identical to healthy state, making ''self-improving'' unfalsifiable.'
  - 'Enforcement scorecard: 1 REAL (Stop hook .purpose/portal), 1 BYPASSABLE (orchestration-required, default warn), 6 THEATER. The .orchestrated marker that ''satisfies enforcement'' is written on tool ENTRY (orchestration.ts:901) before any agent runs — a single mode=quick ping checks the box. Enforcement verifies invocation, not work.'
  - Cid is inert because he owns no durable artifact; brief/debrief are read-only passes over other agents' files. The orchestration DAG is computed, persisted as status:pending, and never updated or read again. Salvageable ONLY by giving him the live task board (claimant + DAG progress + ripple-ranked briefing), else bench honestly.
  - 'Framework-bug: notebook concept keys stored as ''symbol:x'' but queried as bare slug ''x'' — exact-equality match fails, relevantEntries is structurally always 0. Filed T-2026-06-13-001.'
  - 'The task-system audit and orchestration audit found the same hole from two sides: a persisted claimant-owned task DAG closes the learning loop, connects orchestration↔tasks, and gives Cid his artifact — one keystone, four problems.'
