body: |-
  Session 2026-06-13. Matt opened a "mega audit" spree aiming to surface a v7. Slice 1 = the task system; slice 2 = the orchestration engine (chosen because it's the meta-system running all other audits, and Matt flagged "I never see Cid do anything" + "do our own checks actually prove true").

  Method: overrode the auto-orchestrator (which misclassified both analysis tasks as bugfix and proposed build rosters) and hand-assembled 5-lens analysis panels — Arky(architect), North(product), Loid(forge), Cid(captain self-audit), Jinx(advocate). All findings file:line-grounded and cross-confirmed.

  v7 thesis (decision TD-2026-06-13-718): "Close the loop." Three pillars — THE SPINE (persisted claimant-owned task DAG, orchestration emits it, Cid captains it, task_done feeds learning), THE FRONT DOOR (honest classification + all agents routable + fail-visible), THE TEETH (enforcement verifies completion not invocation + falsifiable learning-liveness metric). Free and in-framework; cloud-SaaS/billing/two-way-GitHub-sync parked behind real-external-demand gate; generic PM chrome (due dates/sprints/SLAs/time-tracking) is bloat.

  Matt's durable preference confirmed: wants the complete fix, not the 80/20. Chose "capture, then design the keystone." Next: full design pass on the keystone (task DAG schema with claimant union, orchestration emission, Cid's paradigm_captain_board, typed AgentRelay handoff, task_done→postflight wiring), then adversarial review, then build.
